  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "decompressRow",
    "file": "librawspeed/src/librawspeed/decompressors/SamsungV2Decompressor.cpp",
    "description": "SamsungV2Decompressor::decompressRow performs unchecked neighbor-pixel reads when motion prediction mode is used. In the motion!=7 path it computes refpixel as img_up/img_up2 + i + slideOffset (+/-1) and may also read *(refpixel+2), but there is no bounds check for left/right edges of the row. For slideOffset=-4/-2 or +2/+4 and edge i values, refpixel points before/after the current row buffer, causing reads from poisoned padding (ASan use-after-poison).",
    "conditions": "Trigger requires SRW compression 32773 (SamsungV2 path) so SrwDecoder::decodeRawInternal constructs SamsungV2Decompressor and calls decompress(). The bitstream must drive decompressRow (notably OptFlags::QP in this PoV) into motion modes other than 7 on rows >=2, with edge blocks where i near 0 or 15 and motion-derived slideOffset causes out-of-row reference access. Width is valid/multiple of 16, so decode proceeds until malformed motion/reference bits produce the OOB read."
  },
